  "notes": "Worked example (fictional building, people and companies).\nThe owner wants AT&T, Verizon and T-Mobile inside the warehouse. A COMPASS XR walk before design (Grid test) found every carrier weak behind the racking. The rooftop donor readings (Pre-survey, Cellular carriers) decide which carriers an off-air booster can serve; each carrier must consent before it goes on the air (47 CFR 20.21(c)).\nThe link budget (Design) passes for AT&T (B2) and Verizon (B13). T-Mobile (B71) fails on purpose: its rooftop donor is below the -95 dBm minimum, and more booster gain only amplifies a weak, noisy signal. Options: aim a donor at another T-Mobile site, ask T-Mobile for a carrier-fed source, or its own small cell.",
